---
/**
 * Every dog park in Delaware, on the seven fields nobody publishes together.
 *
 * Grouped by county with Sussex first, because the beach audience is the one
 * this section is for and Sussex is where they are. Three facts here exist
 * nowhere else in one place: Lums Pond is unfenced AND charges a park entry
 * fee, Tidbury closes on Sundays, and Lewes Unleashed will not let you in
 * without a key fob that arrives by mail.
 */
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ParkCard from "../../../components/ParkCard.astro";
import FlagIcon from "../../../components/FlagIcon.astro";

import parksData from "../../../data/parks.json";
import { COUNTY_ORDER, type Park } from "../../../lib/parks";
import { isVerified, robotsFor } from "../../../lib/verification";

const parks = parksData as Park[];
const verified = parks.filter(isVerified);

// The page is only indexable once at least one record has been confirmed.
const pageGate = { verifiedDate: verified.length ? "confirmed" : null, verifiedSource: verified.length ? "confirmed" : null };

const byCounty = COUNTY_ORDER.map((county) => ({
  county,
  parks: parks.filter((p) => p.county === county),
})).filter((g) => g.parks.length);

const unfenced = parks.filter((p) => p.fenced === false);
const noWater = parks.filter((p) => p.water === false);

const schema = verified.length
  ? [
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "ItemList",
        name: "Dog parks in Delaware",
        itemListElement: verified.map((p, i) => ({
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: i + 1,
          item: {
            "@type": "Place",
            name: p.name,
            address: p.address,
            ...(p.lat && p.lng
              ? { geo: { "@type": "GeoCoordinates", latitude: p.lat, longitude: p.lng } }
              : {}),
          },
        })),
      },
    ]
  : [];
---

<Layout
  title="Delaware dog parks: fenced, water, shade, surface, fee"
  description="Delaware dog parks on the seven fields that decide a trip: fenced, size split, water, shade, surface, fee and hours. Including which four are not fenced."
  robots={robotsFor(pageGate)}
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap pt-11 pb-6">
    <p class="label m-0">Dog parks</p>
    <h1 class="text-[2.5rem] sm:text-[3.3rem] mt-3.5 mb-0 max-w-[15ch] text-marsh">
      Every Delaware dog park, on seven fields
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 mb-0 text-[1.15rem] leading-[1.5] max-w-[54ch]">
      Fenced? Size split? Water? Shade? Surface? Fee? Hours? Those are the seven
      things people complain about after they've driven there, and no existing
      guide publishes them together.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose-field pb-2">
    <h2>Read this first</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      Four of these are <strong>not fenced</strong>, which is the single most
      common way a dog park trip goes wrong — people arrive expecting an
      enclosure and find an open field. Two of them cost money. One is closed on
      Sundays. One is private and you cannot get in on the day.
    </p>

    <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 mt-5 mb-2 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="sign px-4 py-3.5">
        <p class="label m-0 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <FlagIcon icon="alert" class="w-[1em] h-[1em] text-flag-red" />
          Not fenced
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.9rem] leading-snug">
          {unfenced.map((p) => p.name).join(", ") || "None recorded"}.
          Reliable recall required.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="sign px-4 py-3.5">
        <p class="label m-0 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <FlagIcon icon="alert" class="w-[1em] h-[1em] text-flag-red" />
          No water on site
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 mb-0 text-[0.9rem] leading-snug">
          {noWater.map((p) => p.name).join(", ") || "None recorded"}.
          Bring your own and a bowl.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="text-[0.9rem] text-ink-soft max-w-[58ch]">
      Every card shows how many of its seven fields are confirmed. A field
      reading <em>Not confirmed</em> means we haven't checked it — it does not
      mean the park lacks the thing. Google's posted hours usually belong to the
      parent park rather than the dog run inside it, which is why so many of
      these still say not confirmed.
    </p>
  </div>

  {
    byCounty.map(({ county, parks: group }) => (
      <div class="wrap pb-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[1.5rem] font-bold text-marsh border-b-[3px] border-marsh pb-2 mb-5 mt-8">
          {county} County
          <span class="stamp text-ink-soft ms-2">{group.length}</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 breakout">
          {group.map((park) => (
            <ParkCard park={park} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    ))
  }

  <div class="wrap prose-field pb-4">
    <h2>What's missing</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      We have found no confirmed public dog park in Seaford, Laurel, Georgetown,
      Smyrna or Bridgeville. If one exists and we've missed it,
      <a href="/how-we-verify/#corrections">tell us</a>. Banning Regional Park
      and the Limestone Road site are listed by other guides but we have not
      been able to confirm either exists as described, so neither is presented
      as fact.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/dogs/">Beach rules by town — all five, side by side</a></li>
      <li><a href="/how-we-verify/">How we check this, and what we do when we're wrong</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
